{
  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) achieved 0.591 acc, a substantial +10.6% improvement over config_001 (singleprofile, 0.485), establishing that multiprofile aggregation is a strong lever. Image alone (config_010, 0.208) is weak, so the current promising direction is RNA with multiprofile. Uncertainty: we do not yet know whether the aggregation method (avgpool vs transformer) matters, or whether the gain is simply from having multiple profiles regardless of how they are pooled. Question tested: config_003 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding model_setting, profile_setting, and encoder identical to config_002, cleanly isolating the effect of aggregation strategy. Why this is the best next experiment: it is a minimal, controlled extension of the strongest result, directly informs whether we should use transformer aggregation in all future multiprofile and multimodal configurations, and avoids the risk of confounding by simultaneously changing encoder or modality. If transformer substantially outperforms avgpool, it reshapes the design space; if not, we confirm avgpool sufficiency and can pivot to testing alternative RNA encoders or multimodal fusion with confidence."
}

